  "body": "#261 part 2 (show where a refused generation was refused), by the triage's middle ground: a refused generation does not draw a partial path; it **marks the spot its refusal names** and lets the user jump there. Nothing is generated or cached, so nothing refused can post.\n\nFork synced at v0.16.0 (branch made from `vilts/Camcraft` main at 66791aa6, which contains the v0.16.0 tag).\n\n## What changed\n\n- **motion**: `GenError` gains `At { msg, at }` (built with `GenError::invalid_at`), plus `location()` / `map_location()`. It displays exactly like `Invalid`, so no refusal sentence, log line or golden changes. A non-finite spot is dropped, never stored. The enum moved to `machining2d/gen_error.rs`; `face.rs` re-exports it, so every `super::face::GenError` path is untouched.\n- **First adopters** (the refusals that already quoted a coordinate):\n  - Face: the narrow strip between two holes (the #260 shape). The spot is the strip's midpoint on the quoted row, at the cut height; `face_holes::narrow_gap` now also returns that midpoint.\n  - Drill cycle: the R-plane, counterbore, bore-fit and centre-cutting doors (the hole's mouth).\n  - Bore and Thread: the counterbore and fit doors (the hole's mouth).\n  - Plunge law: \"would plunge axially into solid\" (the plunge's bottom).\n- **app**:\n  - `run_job` carries the spot from the generator's frame to world through the op's `TiltedFrame`.\n  - The generate command turns it into `CommandError::MachiningAt { msg, at }`, which reads like `Machining`; `CommandError::location()` returns the spot.\n  - The cross-hole spindle frame (`cross_spindle::in_world`) moves the spot by the same world/local shift it already applies to the sentence.\n  - `plunge_solid`'s reason-appending arm keeps the spot.\n- **ui**:\n  - `State::feedback_at` sits beside the refusal sentence and is read only through `State::refusal_focus()`. That returns `None` as soon as the refusal no longer describes the page: the next command, undo/redo, another op on the page, or a draft edit.\n  - The viewport draws a 3-axis cross at the spot in the colour-vision palette's gouge colour (`path_lines::refusal_mark`). It is twice the size of a warned move's cross, so the two never read alike.\n  - The op page's refusal line becomes a link: the hover says so, and a click centres the camera on the spot (part 1's `frame_at`; view state, no command).\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/261-refused-location.md`.\n\n## How it was tested\n\nPinning tests:\n- `camcraft-motion` lib `machining2d::gen_error::tests::{a_located_refusal_reads_exactly_like_an_invalid_one, a_non_finite_spot_is_dropped_never_shown, the_spot_rides_the_frame_map_and_unlocated_refusals_pass}`\n- `camcraft-motion` `face_holes::the_narrow_strip_refusal_points_at_the_strip`\n- `camcraft-motion` lib `drilling::tests::depth_override_applies_to_every_hole` (now also pins the mouth)\n- `camcraft-app` `refusal_location::{a_refused_hole_names_its_mouth_in_world, the_spot_is_the_hole_the_refusal_is_about, a_refusal_about_no_spot_names_none}`\n- `camcraft-app` lib `operation::cross_spindle::tests::a_located_kernel_refusal_lands_on_the_world_mouth`\n- `camcraft-ui` lib `refusal_focus_tests::{a_refused_generation_marks_its_spot_and_caches_nothing, the_mark_retires_with_the_refusal}`\n- `camcraft-ui` lib `path_lines::tests::a_refused_spot_draws_one_wide_gouge_cross_and_nothing_when_non_finite`\n\nQuick gate (`scripts/gate.ps1 -Tier quick` on 82428410, by a separate gate-runner agent): green.\n- motion: lib plus 36 test binaries, 500 passed, 0 failed.\n- app: lib plus 114 test binaries (`center_cut_multiaxis` included), 1091 passed, 0 failed.\n- ui: lib plus 11 test binaries, 488 passed, 0 failed (pixel snapshots ignored, as in quick).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --tests -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- No golden changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The op-page link click in a live window. The link is a plain clickable `egui::Label` with a hover hint (`REFUSAL_LINK_HINT`) that calls the same `frame_at` part 1's warning links use. `refusal_focus` and the overlay are pinned at state level; there is no kittest click test.\n- A located refusal under a real 3+2 tilt: the frame map is `TiltedFrame::to_world`, already covered by its own tests, and the call site is one line in `run_job`.\n- No pixel snapshot changes (snapshots are release-lane).\n\n## Left open\n\n- The other ~620 refusal sites that name no spot yet. They adopt one by one (swap `GenError::Invalid(format!(..))` for `GenError::invalid_at(format!(..), spot)`); follow-up issue #677.\n- Drawing the partial path a generator built before it refused stays out of scope (the triage's \"large, and a design call\"). That's why this PR says `Refs`: the maintainer decides whether #261 closes with this or stays open for that.\n\nChangelog: A refused toolpath generation now marks the spot it names in the viewport, and its message on the operation page jumps there (#261 part 2)\n\nRefs #261\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
